==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Wyvern Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Wyvern and Alec''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
This unit works in a similar way to [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], with better stats in exchange for cost and recharge time. Overall, Wyvern can handle on its own more things than Pizza, but it can't be stacked or replaced easily despite having a below average cooldown time for an uber. For these reasons, this unit is not recommended in presence of [[Tackey]] or [[Director Kurosawah|Kurosawah]]. Additionally, Pizza, despite his short range, still handles Black pushers just as fine and can be given a wave attack talent to hit enemies that both usually cannot. With low range and subpar stats as well, Wyvern is often left without a proper use, being outclassed even by [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] (450 range) in that regard.

===True Form===
Wyvern's true form mainly addresses the issue of survivability by doubling his HP and a 50% chance to weaken all Dark enemies in range. While the weaken is somewhat luck-dependent, the uptime is over 100%, which can be helpful with a decently fast attack rate. This, combined with the Massive Damage from earlier, lets Wyvern act as solid support against Black swarms by knocking them back with sheer damage and slowing their pushing power. However, his range of 370 limits him to melee enemies such as [[Gory Dark]] and [[Dark Otter]], as even his increased HP means little to the backliners still out-of-reach. Additionally, the luck-based weaken effect means that Wyvern can act as supplemental damage and CC to Dark enemies, though his stats still relegate him to supporting other anti-Dark attackers and crowd-controllers.

He also gains Colossus Slayer, which only really has an effect against [[Le'Grim]]. This stat increase against Colossus, alongside decently high HP and weaken effect, let him take some serious damage while dealing it back with the combined effects of Massive Damage and Colossus Slayer. The range disadvantage and luck-dependence are still issues, but they are not major issues since Le'Grim is already considered to be one of the easiest Colossal enemies anyhow.

